From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:47:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(food): several photos per meal, meal type and day, and
 how much was eaten

- One meal can carry up to four photos (camera one by one, or a multi-select
  gallery pick); all go to Claude in a single request, which is told they are
  one meal so each food is counted once.
- Every meal has a type (breakfast, mid-morning, lunch, afternoon snack,
  dinner, nibbles), guessed from Spanish meal hours and changeable; the day
  can be moved to yesterday or any past date, keeping the time of day.
- Each item has an "eaten" fraction (1/4 to x2) over the served portion; the
  stored numbers are what was eaten, the sheet reopens at the whole portion.
  The prompt also tells Claude to follow a note like "half the steak".
- The Food tab groups each day by meal with per-meal totals; the coach line
  gains a per-meal breakdown. Old logs read unchanged (single thumb, meal
  from the clock, eaten 1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
